<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Deliberately EMPTY.

  This is part of the "no paid developer account" plan: every entitlement listed
  here must be provisable by a *free* personal Apple ID when Xcode does
  free-provisioning, otherwise the build fails with
  "provisioning profile doesn't include the ... entitlement".

  Therefore AirChat for iOS uses only entitlement-free frameworks:
    * Network.framework (NWListener)   -> the HTTP + WebSocket server
    * MultipeerConnectivity             -> the mesh (no entitlement required)
    * CoreLocation / CoreMotion         -> compass
    * AVFoundation                      -> voice notes + background keep-alive
    * UIKit / WKWebView                 -> the chat UI itself

  Explicitly NOT used (they all need a paid membership or an Apple approval):
    - Access Wi-Fi Information  (SSID lookup)  -> we read IPs with getifaddrs() instead
    - Hotspot Configuration     (join a Wi-Fi) -> not needed, the host IS the network
    - Personal Hotspot control  (does not exist on iOS at all, paid or not)
    - App Groups / Push / Sign in with Apple
-->
<dict/>
</plist>
